{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dependence-free-batch-b-reviewer-fable-18", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:6a3bc02816cb70ee4042", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The data description designates the well as the independent unit and states that the six rounds per well are repeated, non-independent measurements that should be reduced to one value per well before comparison.", "observed_value": "Independent unit column: well_id; 18 wells x 6 rounds = 108 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "One row is: one water sample drawn from one monitoring well on one survey round\nIndependent unit column: well_id"}, {"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "The eighteen wells are the independent units of the study. The six rounds\nrecorded for a given well are repeated measurements of the same piece of aquifer\nand are not independent of one another, so an analysis that reports a claim about\nthe restoration should reduce each well to a single value"}]}, {"description": "The workflow collapses each well's repeated rounds to a single baseline-to-post change score before any inference, so each independent unit enters the tested dataset exactly once.", "observed_value": "collapse_to_wells produces one change score per well_id (18 scores)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 36, "end_line": 43, "quoted_text": "def collapse_to_wells(readings):\n    \"\"\"One paired change score per well: post-period mean minus baseline mean.\"\"\"\n    contrasts = []\n    for well in sorted(readings):\n        baseline = readings[well][BASELINE_LABEL]\n        post = readings[well][POST_LABEL]\n        baseline_mean = statistics.fmean(baseline)\n        post_mean = statistics.fmean(post)"}]}, {"description": "The statistical test is an exact binomial sign test applied to the signs of the 18 well-level change scores, not to the 108 sample-level rows.", "observed_value": "binomtest(n_down=15, n_tested=18, 0.5, two-sided)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 70, "end_line": 76, "quoted_text": "    signed = [value for value in changes if value != 0.0]\n    n_tested = len(signed)\n    n_down = sum(1 for value in signed if value < 0.0)\n    n_up = n_tested - n_down\n    n_flat = n_wells - n_tested\n\n    outcome = binomtest(n_down, n_tested, 0.5, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]}, {"description": "The reported selected result claims n = 18 independent well-level change scores with p = 0.007538; independent recomputation of the exact two-sided binomial test for 15 of 18 declines gives 2 x (816+153+18+1)/2^18 = 1976/262144 = 0.007538, confirming the p-value was computed on well-level units, not rows.", "observed_value": "recomputed p = 0.0075378... matches reported p = 0.007538", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 42, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial sign test on 18 independent well-level change scores: 15/18 wells declined (estimated proportion 0.833), p = 0.007538; median well-level change -1.10 mg/L."}]}, {"description": "The well-level change scores in the report table are correctly derived from the raw rows; e.g., W-01 baseline rows (11.2, 10.6, 11.5) mean 11.10 and post rows (9.4, 8.8, 9.7) mean 9.30 give the tabulated change of -1.80, and the direction counts (15 decreases, 3 increases: W-05, W-12, W-16) match the raw data.", "observed_value": "W-01 change -1.80; 15 down / 3 up / 0 tied across 18 wells", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "| W-01 | 3 / 3 | 11.10 | 9.30 | -1.80 | decrease |"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "W-01,6.5,baseline,R1,12,11.2"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 56, "end_line": 56, "quoted_text": "W-01,6.5,post_restoration,R4,215,9.4"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 40, "end_line": 40, "quoted_text": "15 of the 18 wells (83.3%) had a lower mean nitrate concentration after reconnection, 3 had a higher mean, and 0 were unchanged."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The input file does contain six rows per independent unit (e.g., well W-01 appears on six data rows), so repeated entries of each well into the raw table exist and could have fed a row-independent procedure had the workflow skipped aggregation; the code, however, aggregates these rows within read_long_table/collapse_to_wells before testing, so this repetition never reaches the inference.", "observed_value": "6 rows per well_id in data/input.csv; aggregated before binomtest", "source_spans": [{"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "W-01,6.5,baseline,R1,12,11.2"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "W-01,6.5,baseline,R2,40,10.6"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 92, "end_line": 92, "quoted_text": "W-01,6.5,post_restoration,R6,271,9.7"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 46, "end_line": 46, "quoted_text": "The test treats wells, not individual water samples, as replicates. Pooling all 108 sample-level records into a sample-by-sample comparison would count every well 6 times and would overstate the evidence; the reported p-value rests on the 18 well-level scores alone."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to show that the reported p-value could only have come from entering wells repeatedly into a row-independent test. I recomputed the exact two-sided binomial sign test on the 18 well-level signs derived independently from the raw rows: 15 of 18 wells declined, giving p = 2 x (C(18,15)+C(18,16)+C(18,17)+C(18,18))/2^18 = 1976/262144 = 0.007538, which matches the reported p exactly. A row-level version of the analysis would have used n = 108 samples or n = 54 round-level pairs, which cannot reproduce p = 0.007538 with 15/18 declines. I also traced the code path: binomtest receives n_down and n_tested computed from the per-well change scores produced by collapse_to_wells, with no branch that passes sample-level rows into the test, and spot-checked three wells' means and signs against the CSV (all consistent). The falsification failed on every check, so the issue class is not demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}